EXT. FLOODED RIVER - DEBRIS RAFT - DAY

A raft of roof planks and oil drums turns in brown current. A drowned town drifts by: a steeple, a bus stop, a pink bicycle.

CAPTAIN RENATA SOUZA, 40s, scarred forearms, braces a pole. ABEL OKUMU, 17, bails water with a bucket. TRUDY HALVORSEN, 60s, holds a small radio in a freezer bag. A little girl, LENA, 6, hugs a plastic dinosaur and doesn't speak.

RADIO (V.O.)
(static)
...repeat, any survivors on the river, hold position, we're coming...

TRUDY
They're coming!

RENATA
Don't wave the radio, Trudy, keep it dry.

A tree rolls out of the current and strikes the raft. Everyone stumbles. Abel drops the bucket. Trudy loses her grip on the radio bag. Lena falls and the dinosaur skates into the river.

LENA
Rex!

Abel dives for it. Renata grabs his collar. The dinosaur bobs once, twice, and Abel reaches out his whole length, grabs it, and slaps it back into Lena's arms.

ABEL
Got him.

Lena says nothing. She just holds him tight.

RADIO (V.O.)
(static)
...we can see you...

A helicopter thunders over the trees. All four of them look up. Nobody speaks.
